WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.137
[Caroline] Since we can't

00:00:01.137 --> 00:00:02.171
 travel in person,

00:00:02.171 --> 00:00:04.073
we created "Share Your World,"

00:00:04.073 --> 00:00:05.975
a show where fellow travel lovers

00:00:05.975 --> 00:00:07.877
and I share experiences from

00:00:07.877 --> 00:00:09.579
our cultural backgrounds.

00:00:09.579 --> 00:00:10.680
In this episode, we're

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.882
saving room for desserts.

00:00:18.888 --> 00:00:20.356
[Caroline] Some save it for 
the end of the meal,

00:00:20.356 --> 00:00:22.358
and others skip straight to it.

00:00:22.358 --> 00:00:25.194
No matter how you enjoy them,
desserts are a sweet form

00:00:25.194 --> 00:00:27.797
of comfort food served around the world.

00:00:27.797 --> 00:00:30.233
My favorite Armenian dessert is Gata.

00:00:30.233 --> 00:00:32.969
It's a sweet, round pastry.

00:00:32.969 --> 00:00:35.438
And it's just really good
when you have it with tea,

00:00:35.438 --> 00:00:38.908
or in the morning as breakfast,
or just a pastry on its own.

00:00:38.908 --> 00:00:42.011
Also, with gata, sometimes the bakers

00:00:42.011 --> 00:00:43.913
put a little coin in there,

00:00:43.913 --> 00:00:46.282
and whoever gets the slice

00:00:46.282 --> 00:00:48.918
with the coin is said to have good luck.

00:00:48.918 --> 00:00:51.988
So I remember as a kid, I
would always eat so much,

00:00:51.988 --> 00:00:55.291
just so I can get the coin
and I can get the good luck.

00:00:55.291 --> 00:00:58.394
If you go to villages,
like Garni and Geghard,

00:00:58.394 --> 00:01:01.164
those women over there
make it a certain way.

00:01:01.164 --> 00:01:03.166
And they usually put Armenian letters

00:01:03.166 --> 00:01:06.069
over it, or they write Geghard,

00:01:06.069 --> 00:01:08.771
which is the place that they are from.

00:01:08.771 --> 00:01:09.405
[Jason] So one of my

00:01:09.405 --> 00:01:10.673
favorite Cambodian desserts

00:01:10.673 --> 00:01:12.642
is sticky rice with

00:01:12.642 --> 00:01:14.077
mango and coconut milk.

00:01:14.077 --> 00:01:15.645
I actually went to Cambodia,

00:01:15.645 --> 00:01:17.747
and my uncle owns a restaurant

00:01:17.747 --> 00:01:19.749
where he actually made the dessert for me.

00:01:19.749 --> 00:01:21.384
So, the mango is not your typical mango.

00:01:21.384 --> 00:01:23.486
It's this long yellow mango,

00:01:23.486 --> 00:01:25.688
as opposed to the green and red one.

00:01:25.688 --> 00:01:29.692
And it's more like ovally-shaped
than the round circle.

00:01:29.692 --> 00:01:33.229
When you eat foods that have
emotional connections to it,

00:01:33.229 --> 00:01:35.264
I think it does taste better.
So every time I eat it now,

00:01:35.264 --> 00:01:39.535
again, I remember my time in Cambodia.

00:01:40.803 --> 00:01:42.071
[Kasey] So whenever I visit

00:01:42.071 --> 00:01:45.041
Korea, the first thing I do is

00:01:45.041 --> 00:01:47.176
I go get this dessert called patbingsu.

00:01:47.176 --> 00:01:50.413
It's a shaved ice, it's about yea high.

00:01:50.413 --> 00:01:52.982
They put condensed milk,
they put fruit pieces.

00:01:52.982 --> 00:01:55.485
They put mochi rice cakes, red bean,

00:01:55.485 --> 00:01:59.422
and you can get matcha
flavor, vanilla, hazelnut.

00:01:59.422 --> 00:02:03.693
It's so refreshing and much,
much lighter than ice cream.

00:02:03.693 --> 00:02:05.695
So the last time I went
to visit my parents,

00:02:05.695 --> 00:02:08.631
I stayed at the JW
Marriott Hotel in Seoul.

00:02:08.631 --> 00:02:10.767
And it's near this 
neighborhood called Myeong-dong

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:13.069
And they just have all
these street vendors

00:02:13.069 --> 00:02:15.304
late at night, and a ton of food options.

00:02:15.304 --> 00:02:17.807
And there's a ton of shopping in the area.

00:02:17.807 --> 00:02:20.743
So I will drag my parents
out at 11, midnight.

00:02:20.743 --> 00:02:23.646
And we will go stop by all
the little street vendors.

00:02:23.646 --> 00:02:25.715
And then for a dessert drink,

00:02:25.715 --> 00:02:27.717
there's this sweet rice milk.

00:02:27.717 --> 00:02:28.751
It's not thick at all.

00:02:28.751 --> 00:02:30.887
So it's the consistency of lemonade.

00:02:30.887 --> 00:02:33.322
And it's slightly sweet
and it's refreshing.

00:02:33.322 --> 00:02:36.092
And it has little pieces of rice in it.

00:02:36.092 --> 00:02:38.227
So then at the end, you kind of swirl it

00:02:38.227 --> 00:02:39.495
so you can get all the rice chunks.

00:02:39.495 --> 00:02:41.364
Even though I like to
buy the sweet rice drink,

00:02:41.364 --> 00:02:43.833
I always want my mom to
make a whole batch as well.

00:02:43.833 --> 00:02:46.135
So I'll use my Marriott
Bonvoy Boundless™ Card

00:02:46.135 --> 00:02:49.572
to earn points by buying
all the ingredients.

00:02:49.572 --> 00:02:51.040
So it's so beneficial because I'm

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:53.709
spending it on the card,
but also earning points.

00:02:53.709 --> 00:02:54.544
So I just feel like it all

00:02:54.544 --> 00:02:56.646
works out great, having this card.

00:02:56.646 --> 00:02:59.582
I will travel anywhere just
to try all the best desserts,

00:02:59.582 --> 00:03:01.551
the best snacks, the best meals.

00:03:01.551 --> 00:03:02.819
I'm all about it.

00:03:02.819 --> 00:03:05.288
You know, to me, food is also art.

00:03:05.288 --> 00:03:06.389
[Katrina] I'm with you on that.

00:03:06.389 --> 00:03:11.260
Plus one on the foodie, I
will travel for food as well.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.728
[Debby] Honestly, when I was younger,

00:03:12.728 --> 00:03:14.163
my biggest dream was

00:03:14.163 --> 00:03:15.598
working in a Swiss bakery

00:03:15.598 --> 00:03:18.167
because I just love every bit

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:20.002
of pastry that we have back home.

00:03:20.002 --> 00:03:22.405
And when you go to a Swiss bakery

00:03:22.405 --> 00:03:25.808
the way they present it, it's
just absolutely beautiful.

00:03:25.808 --> 00:03:27.443
Two of my favorite pastries, which,

00:03:27.443 --> 00:03:29.312
I mean you have it here
in America as well,

00:03:29.312 --> 00:03:32.114
it's carrot cake and a Black Forest cake.

00:03:32.114 --> 00:03:33.716
We can buy it here in America,

00:03:33.716 --> 00:03:35.952
but it's just obviously
not the same recipe.

00:03:35.952 --> 00:03:37.487
It's different back home.

00:03:37.487 --> 00:03:39.455
So the chocolate that's on
top of the Black Forest cake

00:03:39.455 --> 00:03:43.726
in Switzerland is just this
very thinly sliced chocolate,

00:03:43.726 --> 00:03:46.963
and inside the Black Forest
cake, there's dark cherries.

00:03:46.963 --> 00:03:48.531
And I think here in America

00:03:48.531 --> 00:03:50.533
a lot of times it's the
bright red cherries.

00:03:50.533 --> 00:03:54.036
They're just softer and they
have a much richer taste to it.

00:03:54.036 --> 00:03:55.371
The carrot cake back home is really

00:03:55.371 --> 00:03:58.307
just the cake base with carrots in it.

00:03:58.307 --> 00:04:01.944
And then the top is a sugary glaze

00:04:01.944 --> 00:04:02.778
that you make yourself,

00:04:02.778 --> 00:04:04.580
you can add some lemon to it for flavor.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:08.317
And then we actually have
little carrot shaped marzipans

00:04:08.317 --> 00:04:10.219
that we decorate it with.

00:04:10.219 --> 00:04:11.554
I literally can't get enough of it.

00:04:11.554 --> 00:04:13.422
So whenever I go to Switzerland,

00:04:13.422 --> 00:04:16.659
you bet I'm gonna eat those things.

00:04:16.659 --> 00:04:17.827
[Caroline] Yeah, like with Switzerland,

00:04:17.827 --> 00:04:19.462
you know you're gonna try chocolate,

00:04:19.462 --> 00:04:24.100
but no one told me I should
try the carrot cake too.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.334
[Debby] Yeah because as I said,

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:27.336
in America you know carrot cake.

00:04:27.336 --> 00:04:28.671
So it's not something that you would

00:04:28.671 --> 00:04:30.439
necessarily try in a different country,

00:04:30.439 --> 00:04:32.441
because it's not specific to Switzerland.

00:04:32.441 --> 00:04:34.944
It's just the way that
we make it is different.

00:04:34.944 --> 00:04:36.445
We're surrounded by a bunch of countries.

00:04:36.445 --> 00:04:37.914
There's Germany, there's
France, there's Italy.

00:04:37.914 --> 00:04:41.784
It's a very small country,
but very, very international.

00:04:41.784 --> 00:04:44.520
So we do like to borrow ideas

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:47.857
and recipes from our
surrounding countries.

00:04:47.857 --> 00:04:50.993
[Caroline] I am so hungry
after our conversation.

00:04:50.993 --> 00:04:53.029
I definitely learned a lot.

00:04:53.029 --> 00:04:56.866
And I can't wait to try
everything that we talked about.

00:04:56.866 --> 00:04:59.635
If you got a sweet tooth
from watching this video,

00:04:59.635 --> 00:05:01.771
we hope you're inspired to start planning

00:05:01.771 --> 00:05:04.307
your next dessert-filled adventure.

